{"availability":"available","full":"elboletaire/password-strength-meter","name":"password-strength-meter","description":":key: A password strength meter","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":107,"forks":42,"created":"2017-03-11T16:57:36Z","updated":"2026-10-09T15:26:01Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"https://elboletaire.github.io/password-strength-meter/","topics":["javascript","jquery","jquery-plugin","password","password-security","password-strength","password-strength-meter","plugin","react","svelte","vanilla-javascript","vue","vuejs"],"demo":"https://elboletaire.github.io/password-strength-meter/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:34.926Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:34.926Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:34.926Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T19:51:34.926Z","stars":107,"forks":42}],"technologies":["React","Vue","Svelte"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Accessible password strength meters for every framework, built on one small core.","About the name. Passcore is the name of the packages (@passcore/). It plays on pass score (the score of a password, written with one s because \"passscore\" repeated too many letters) and on core (the small core every package shares). This repository is still called password-strength-meter because that is how it started: as a jQuery plugin with that name. The original password-strength-meter package on npm is now a compatibility release; see Looking for the old plugin?."],"features":["Length first. The estimate counts how hard a password is to guess, and discounts repeats, sequences, keyboard runs, common passwords and personal details such as the username. Adding characters never makes a password…","Rules are separate from strength. Minimum length, required character types, \"no personal details\" and \"not a common password\" are configurable and reported on their own, so a long passphrase that misses one rule still…","Accessible. A role=\"meter\" bar with ARIA values, and the message in a polite live region linked to the input.","Translated, your way. The core returns message keys, never texts. English, Spanish and Catalan are included in i18next's JSON format (see locales/), and you can pass your own translate function, such as i18next's t.","Themeable. One stylesheet, colored with CSS custom properties, no images."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/elboletaire/password-strength-meter/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"a2a67c5d9d9662be0afea65274ebd89ab54cb012c84a925c5130525fac309749","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:35.066Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:35.066Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Accessible password strength meters for every framework, built on one small core.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/elboletaire/password-strength-meter/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"a2a67c5d9d9662be0afea65274ebd89ab54cb012c84a925c5130525fac309749","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/elboletaire/password-strength-meter/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:35.066Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-09T15:26:01Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/elboletaire/password-strength-meter/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:35.067Z","hash":"a2a67c5d9d9662be0afea65274ebd89ab54cb012c84a925c5130525fac309749","originalBytes":5517,"storedBytes":5517,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["passcore","packages","jquery","core","npm","password","pnpm","package","react","one","plugin","build","each","own","playground","svelte","vue","component","every","import","message","meter","old","onchange","options","password-strength-meter","vanilla","accessible","bash","because","common","compatibility","const","createmeter","custom","details","dev","different","function","how","i18next","length","live","locales","look","looking","name.","never","now","only","pass","personal","readme"